WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.100
<v Pledgivo>Connect your payment account

2
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:52.075
<v Payments>Step 0 — collect three keys — Two restricted keys and a publishable key, all from one gateway screen

3
00:00:52.075 --> 00:01:21.275
<v Payments>Step 1 — the external credential, twice — Custom protocol; one credential for the public site, one for the back office

4
00:01:21.275 --> 00:03:02.275
<v Payments>Step 2 — the principal, and the secret — Named Principal, one authentication parameter, holding the key

5
00:03:02.275 --> 00:03:22.800
<v Payments>Step 3 — the Authorization header — A merge formula, not a value — the key never appears here

6
00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:55.680
<v Payments>Steps 4 to 6 — the named credential — Point it at the gateway, allow the package namespace, formulas on

7
00:03:55.680 --> 00:05:07.000
<v Payments>Step 7 — let your staff use it — Principal access plus User External Credential, read and create

8
00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:25.125
<v Payments>Step 8 — let your public site use it — The donor credential's permission set goes onto the guest user

9
00:05:25.125 --> 00:05:52.005
<v Payments>Step 9 — the payment account record — Name the two named credentials, paste the publishable key, choose the mode

10
00:05:52.005 --> 00:06:25.155
<v Payments>Steps 10 and 11 — the two live checks — One passed, one failed — and the failure is the point

11
00:06:25.155 --> 00:06:43.385
<v Wrap up>Nothing is connected until it is tested.

12
00:06:43.385 --> 00:07:09.485
<v About Pledgivo>Fundraising and donation management, native to Salesforce. Docs: pledgivo.cloudalgo.com

